from __future__ import annotations
import json

EDITORIAL_PAGES = json.loads(r'''{"agriculture":{"intro":"Agriculture decisions work best when production economics, environmental conditions and market requirements are considered together. This guide connects crop and livestock planning with water, genetics, horticulture and traceable value chains, without claiming that a particular farm or service is currently operating.","chapters":[{"title":"From the farm question to a decision model","text":"Begin with a defined production unit and an explicit objective: cost per unit, margin, water productivity or quality. Separate fixed assets from variable inputs, record labor honestly and build alternative weather and price assumptions before choosing a production plan.","steps":["List crops or livestock enterprises, area, expected yield and production cycle.","Calculate input requirements, cash-flow timing and break-even conditions.","Compare a baseline, a constrained-water scenario and a market-price shock."]},{"title":"Crops, horticulture and genetic improvement","text":"Orchards, greenhouse systems and field crops require different calendars, irrigation methods, protection plans and harvest handling. When evaluating plant varieties or animal breeds, compare locally relevant traits, disease resistance, genetic diversity and regulatory requirements—not just headline yields.","steps":["Identify soil, climate, water and biological constraints for each production system.","Document variety or breed selection criteria and the source of agronomic claims.","Plan monitoring of growth, health, input use and product quality."]},{"title":"From harvest to responsible market access","text":"A profitable farm enterprise depends on losses after harvest, grading, storage conditions, transport, packaging and buyer requirements. Record assumptions and test the full value chain with small pilots before promising revenue or capacity.","steps":["Map every handling step and its cost, quality risk and accountable owner.","Define grading, storage and traceability requirements for the target market.","Pilot an auditable cost-and-quality sheet before scaling."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"What is a farm feasibility study?","answer":"It compares technical constraints, production costs, sales assumptions and risks over a defined period. It should show the evidence behind each yield and price assumption, not a guaranteed return."},{"question":"How should a new variety be selected?","answer":"Evaluate its performance under comparable local conditions, verified disease resistance, water needs, available seed or stock, and relevant approvals. Small controlled trials can reduce uncertainty."}],"links":[{"label":"Research methods","url":"/research/"},{"label":"Digital market","url":"/market/"},{"label":"Agricultural venture","url":"/ventures/agriculture/"}]},"industry":{"intro":"Industrial product development starts long before factory equipment is purchased. This guide explains how to turn a customer problem into a documented specification, a reproducible production process and a responsible market launch.","chapters":[{"title":"Discover the actual customer requirement","text":"Use interviews, complaints, observed workflows and competitive alternatives to define the job a product must perform. Convert broad ideas into measurable requirements such as tolerance, safety, lifespan, operating cost and repairability.","steps":["Write a one-page product brief with measurable acceptance criteria.","Separate legally required standards from optional features.","Record assumptions that still require user or technical validation."]},{"title":"Prototype, production and quality systems","text":"Move from concept to small batches with version-controlled drawings, a bill of materials and acceptance tests. Check sourcing and process capability before making volume commitments. Prevent defects by designing inspection into the workflow.","steps":["Build a prototype and log test failures with corrective actions.","Map materials, suppliers, equipment, maintenance and operator tasks.","Specify batch records, traceability and inspection checkpoints."]},{"title":"Commercial readiness and lifecycle cost","text":"A viable industrial product also requires support, packaging, logistics, warranties and clear terms. Evaluate both unit economics and the costs of returns, quality failures and regulatory compliance.","steps":["Estimate cost of goods, overhead allocation and support requirements.","Test shipping protection, labeling and product documentation.","Release only after technical and customer acceptance evidence is reviewed."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"What should be completed before tooling?","answer":"A stable specification, verified prototype, target cost, safety review and sourcing plan reduce expensive changes after tooling."},{"question":"Does a working prototype prove readiness for mass production?","answer":"No. Repeatability, manufacturing yield, process capability, supply assurance and service support must also be demonstrated."}],"links":[{"label":"Research","url":"/research/"},{"label":"Market planning","url":"/market/"},{"label":"Economics","url":"/economy/"}]},"research":{"intro":"Credible research is defined by transparent questions, trustworthy evidence and limits that readers can inspect. Moj Play Win presents research methods, digital experimentation and practical translation of findings into usable work.","chapters":[{"title":"Frame a question that can be answered","text":"Translate a broad theme into a population, setting, outcome and comparison where appropriate. Define what would count as disconfirming evidence as well as a successful result.","steps":["Write a research question, scope and intended audience.","Choose measurable outcomes and a sampling or case-selection method.","Register assumptions, constraints, permissions and a clear decision point."]},{"title":"Evaluate and document evidence","text":"Search systematically, record publication dates, compare study designs and distinguish observation from causal evidence. Assess bias, missing data and conflicts of interest before drawing conclusions.","steps":["Maintain a searchable source and evidence register.","Record methods, data origin, uncertainty and key counterarguments.","Keep analysis code or calculations reproducible when permitted."]},{"title":"Publish an actionable report","text":"A practical report needs an abstract, methods, findings, limitations and recommendations proportionate to the quality of its evidence. Protect sensitive data and do not imply peer review unless it occurred.","steps":["Prepare an executive summary with the major findings.","Give readers methods, definitions and reproducibility notes.","Identify decisions supported by evidence and questions that remain open."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"What makes a research claim credible?","answer":"A clear method, reliable sources, appropriate analysis and explicit uncertainty help readers judge its strength. Strong presentation alone is not evidence."},{"question":"Can AI replace verification?","answer":"No. AI can help organize material, but source checking, factual validation and responsibility for conclusions remain essential."}],"links":[{"label":"Knowledge library","url":"/knowledge/"},{"label":"AI tools","url":"/agents/"},{"label":"Company","url":"/company/"}]},"knowledge":{"intro":"A useful knowledge library does more than list articles. It connects definitions, practical examples and trustworthy sources so readers can move from a beginner's question to a deeper, testable understanding.","chapters":[{"title":"Learn from concepts to application","text":"Start with common vocabulary and an example of the problem. Explain necessary background before adding advanced terminology. Distinguish general learning resources from paid or formally certified instruction.","steps":["Define the audience and three learning outcomes.","Introduce key terms and a worked real-world example.","Add a short self-check or application exercise."]},{"title":"Judge the quality of sources","text":"Compare primary research, official technical documents and secondary explanations. Check publication dates, context and whether findings are generalizable. Preserve provenance when the content is updated.","steps":["Record the original source, author and date when available.","Identify disagreements, limitations and out-of-date recommendations.","Review examples and links for accessibility and accuracy."]},{"title":"Turn learning into a reusable resource","text":"Structured notes, checklists and worked templates are more useful than disconnected summaries. Review the materials after feedback and keep revisions traceable.","steps":["Publish an overview, practical method and expected output.","Provide a reading path from introductory to advanced topics.","Maintain a change log for substantive corrections."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Is every page a certified course?","answer":"No. Informational guides are not accreditation or evidence that an instructor-led course is active. Any formal credential must be clearly described and verified."},{"question":"How do I use the library for a project?","answer":"Start with a problem statement, collect authoritative background, apply the relevant checklist and document what needs specialist validation."}],"links":[{"label":"Research","url":"/research/"},{"label":"Studio","url":"/studio/"},{"label":"Digital store","url":"/store/"}]},"economy":{"intro":"Economic intelligence should help readers understand incentives, production systems and uncertainty without promising market outcomes. This page describes practical methods for assessing costs, prices, trade-offs and potential risks.","chapters":[{"title":"Read the structure behind a market","text":"Separate supply constraints, demand, policy, logistics and exchange-rate exposure. Choose meaningful time periods and avoid mixing nominal values with inflation-adjusted comparisons.","steps":["State the market, geography, unit of measure and date.","Distinguish official data, industry estimates and working assumptions.","Document seasonal effects and comparability limits."]},{"title":"Test scenarios instead of predicting certainty","text":"Build transparent base, upside and downside cases for revenues, costs and working capital. Explain which input drives each case and what evidence would justify changing it.","steps":["Model changes in input costs, demand and payment delays.","Measure break-even, liquidity needs and sensitivity to assumptions.","Present risks and response options without guaranteed forecasts."]},{"title":"Translate analysis into business decisions","text":"Economic reports are useful when they connect observations to procurement, pricing, inventory or product decisions. Show how to update a decision when better evidence arrives.","steps":["Identify the decision owner, review horizon and data sources.","Compare options using costs, reversibility and downside exposure.","Schedule regular source review and note material changes."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Are the numbers on this page live market quotes?","answer":"No. This page is a methodology guide, not a real-time price or foreign-exchange feed. Time-sensitive figures must be separately sourced, dated and verified."},{"question":"Does scenario analysis guarantee profit?","answer":"No. It clarifies the effect of assumptions and uncertainty; it cannot eliminate market or execution risk."}],"links":[{"label":"Industry","url":"/industry/"},{"label":"Market","url":"/market/"},{"label":"Research","url":"/research/"}]},"studio":{"intro":"Original digital experiences are developed through playable prototypes, honest usability testing and sustainable production processes. This guide covers the journey from an interactive idea to a documented game or creative digital release.","chapters":[{"title":"Design the core experience","text":"A game begins with a decision the player makes and feedback that makes the consequence understandable. Define the intended audience and accessibility needs before expanding the level count or visual effects.","steps":["Write a one-sentence experience promise and player goal.","Prototype a complete three-to-five-minute interaction loop.","Observe fresh players and note confusion without coaching them."]},{"title":"Build, test and iterate","text":"Record versioned builds, input methods, performance budgets, audio and visual rights, and accessibility checks. Measure the experience on target devices, including low-powered mobile hardware.","steps":["Test touch, keyboard, pauses, subtitles and reduced motion.","Log crashes, input latency, progress blockers and inconsistent outcomes.","Fix core usability before adding cosmetic scope."]},{"title":"Prepare truthful release information","text":"Describe the actual supported platforms, required permissions, pricing and content limitations. Use screenshots of tested features, clearly labeling any conceptual promotional art.","steps":["Create a build manifest and instructions for first use.","Prepare store text, accessibility notes and support contact path.","Verify entitlements and downloads only when a commerce system is active."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Are all listed game ideas playable today?","answer":"No. A concept, prototype and released title are different stages. Product pages should show the verified status rather than using an untested Play button."},{"question":"Why test on older phones?","answer":"Performance, legibility and controls can behave differently on low-memory or smaller devices, affecting real-world access."}],"links":[{"label":"Knowledge","url":"/knowledge/"},{"label":"Market","url":"/market/"},{"label":"Research","url":"/research/"}]},"market":{"intro":"A reliable digital market helps a customer understand a product before making a financial commitment. Browse concepts, learning resources and service categories with clear distinctions between informational pages and verified active offers.","chapters":[{"title":"Create a complete product record","text":"Each actual offer needs a specific title, audience, delivery format, version, requirements, price and license. Editorial cards are not substitutes for the authoritative product database.","steps":["Verify the exact file or service deliverable and its availability.","List compatible devices, language, limitations and licensing terms.","Use distinct product images and accurate previews when available."]},{"title":"Make the purchase path trustworthy","text":"A secure checkout should present the amount, currency, supported methods and next steps. A successful redirect alone is not proof that payment reconciliation and digital delivery work.","steps":["Check authoritative product ID, price and the active payment route.","Verify payment confirmation, idempotency and error recovery.","Confirm access, downloads, receipts and support after purchase."]},{"title":"Measure customer success responsibly","text":"Build around product usefulness, delivery reliability and transparent support rather than exaggerated claims. Review abandoned sessions and service problems without exposing private customer data.","steps":["Check broken links and incomplete catalog descriptions.","Collect actionable feedback on delivery and instructions.","Update only verified offerings while preserving existing orders and rights."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Can I buy every item mentioned?","answer":"Not necessarily. Some entries are educational or product concepts. Checkout should appear only where an actual verified offer and delivery mechanism exist."},{"question":"Are cryptocurrencies required?","answer":"The purchase methods for an actual product are shown on its verified checkout page. This guide does not modify or promise any payment method."}],"links":[{"label":"Digital store","url":"/store/"},{"label":"Company","url":"/company/"},{"label":"Knowledge","url":"/knowledge/"}]},"agents":{"intro":"AI is valuable when a narrowly defined task can be evaluated against trustworthy evidence. This resource explains practical assistant design, privacy, human oversight and the distinction between a demonstrated feature and a running production agent.","chapters":[{"title":"Define a useful assistant task","text":"Begin with a repeatable user need, well-scoped inputs and a testable output. Create representative examples and clear criteria for unacceptable answers and unsafe actions.","steps":["Write the task boundary and permitted data sources.","Build a test set with typical and adversarial cases.","Specify when a human must review, approve or stop an action."]},{"title":"Control tools, information and privacy","text":"Assistants should use the minimum permissions required and identify uncertain or outdated information. Restrict secrets, customer records, financial actions and cross-user retrieval.","steps":["Validate identity and access for every retrieved resource.","Log essential actions without duplicating sensitive content.","Test unsupported requests, failures and prompt-injection resistance."]},{"title":"Operate with measurable evidence","text":"A code definition or successful unit test does not prove that a worker is active. Production claims require health checks, real run histories, owner-visible status and failure recovery.","steps":["Measure task completion, latency, quality and error categories.","Verify actual runtime heartbeat and a traceable completed task.","Document escalation and safe rollback for every automation."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Does this page mean the AI agents are running?","answer":"No. It describes capabilities and quality criteria. Active operation must be proven separately by a recent real runtime heartbeat and successful tasks."},{"question":"Should AI make autonomous financial decisions?","answer":"Sensitive financial or external actions require appropriate authorization, auditability, safeguards and independent verification."}],"links":[{"label":"Research","url":"/research/"},{"label":"Knowledge","url":"/knowledge/"},{"label":"Company","url":"/company/"}]},"company":{"intro":"Moj Play Win brings together a proposed digital-first portfolio centered on research, games, learning and modern technology, alongside selected professional interests in agriculture, craft, hospitality and commerce. This overview describes areas of focus rather than claiming every service is already commercially active.","chapters":[{"title":"Our digital-first direction","text":"The proposed emphasis is approximately 80 percent research, technology, digital products, interactive entertainment and practical education; the remaining portfolio draws on experience across other professional sectors.","steps":["Develop original, testable digital experiences and knowledge products.","Document methods, examples and delivery requirements honestly.","Distinguish prototypes, planned services and live offerings."]},{"title":"Collaboration and project discovery","text":"Useful collaboration begins with a concrete business need, scope, audience, budget range and defined outputs. Work may include research design, web engineering, operational analysis and educational resources, subject to agreement.","steps":["Describe the problem and desired outcome.","Agree on deliverables, milestones, ownership and review criteria.","Assess security, accessibility, privacy and post-launch support."]},{"title":"Professional standards and accountability","text":"Product and research communications should use accurate claims, accessible interfaces, proper intellectual-property permissions and support processes that customers can understand.","steps":["Keep content rights and data handling requirements explicit.","Validate website performance and links on relevant devices.","Maintain a documented review and correction process."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Is the 80/20 portfolio already fully operational?","answer":"It describes a strategic direction and mix of interests, not audited operating revenue or proof that every venture has launched."},{"question":"How do I propose cooperation?","answer":"Prepare a concise project brief covering the audience, required output, scope, timeline and any security or integration constraints; use the company's contact route."}],"links":[{"label":"Research","url":"/research/"},{"label":"Industry","url":"/industry/"},{"label":"Digital store","url":"/store/"}]},"venture:agriculture":{"intro":"Farm and rural-enterprise projects require economic discipline and agronomic evidence. This venture guide brings together field planning, crop and livestock systems, processing economics and responsible commercialization.","chapters":[{"title":"Assess farm resources and constraints","text":"Document land, water rights, soil suitability, labor, equipment and access to services. Compare production systems under real resource constraints instead of assuming best-case yields.","steps":["Build a farm asset and constraints register.","Estimate costs and operating requirements per enterprise.","Compare dry-year and price-change scenarios."]},{"title":"Design resilient crop and livestock programs","text":"Consider rotation, orchard and greenhouse needs, animal nutrition, welfare and genetic diversity as separate specialties that require localized expertise.","steps":["Set indicators for water, soil, animal health and output quality.","Validate technical recommendations with qualified specialists.","Create a monitoring schedule for each production cycle."]},{"title":"Evaluate processing and market channels","text":"Trace losses, sorting, packing, storage and transport against buyer requirements. Assess whether value-added processing improves the margin after capital and operating costs.","steps":["Draw a traceable value-chain map.","Calculate cost per saleable unit including waste and logistics.","Test buyer requirements and product documentation before expansion."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Is this a farm sales listing?","answer":"No. It is a project and knowledge overview; verified farm inventory and sale terms belong on a separate active product listing."},{"question":"Is a universal water plan possible?","answer":"No. Soil, climate, water availability, crop choices and local regulations determine an appropriate design."}],"links":[{"label":"Agriculture","url":"/agriculture/"},{"label":"Research","url":"/research/"}]},"venture:cafe-restaurant":{"intro":"A memorable cafe or restaurant depends on clear positioning and consistently good service, not decoration alone. This guide addresses guest journeys, menu costing, food safety and digital operations without claiming a physical venue.","chapters":[{"title":"Define the hospitality concept","text":"Choose a target guest need, service style, menu scope and appropriate location criteria. Document the practical experience from discovery through payment and feedback.","steps":["Build guest personas and a service blueprint.","Test a concise menu against kitchen capability.","Separate essential operating needs from optional atmosphere upgrades."]},{"title":"Engineer menu and service operations","text":"Recipe costing, allergen documentation, inventory controls and staff training protect margins and guest safety. Adapt policies to applicable food-safety requirements.","steps":["Maintain ingredient specs, allergens and portion yields.","Measure preparation time, waste and menu contribution margins.","Create opening, cleaning and service checklists."]},{"title":"Build useful digital touchpoints","text":"Menus, inquiries, booking information and loyalty systems need actual staff processes behind them. Never label a table or product as available without verified inventory or scheduling.","steps":["Use accessible menus with clearly stated prices and ingredients.","Design a real inquiry and confirmation flow before enabling bookings.","Review customer privacy and after-service feedback handling."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Can I reserve a table here?","answer":"This guide does not represent an operating venue or a live reservation system."},{"question":"Why measure menu contribution?","answer":"A popular item can still lose money after ingredient, labor and waste costs; unit economics inform sustainable pricing."}],"links":[{"label":"Company","url":"/company/"},{"label":"Digital commerce","url":"/ventures/ecommerce/"}]},"venture:fuel-station":{"intro":"Fuel and mobility projects combine regulated operations, safety, customer experience and changing vehicle needs. This page provides planning considerations only and does not describe an active licensed station.","chapters":[{"title":"Study demand and location suitability","text":"Assess traffic patterns, site access, accessibility, nearby services and relevant zoning before proposing a service mix. Operational permission is jurisdiction-dependent.","steps":["Describe likely customer segments and vehicle types.","Review access, queues and emergency-vehicle circulation.","Identify permits, environmental requirements and local specialists."]},{"title":"Develop safety-first operating procedures","text":"Risk management includes hazardous materials, fire prevention, staff training, storage integrity and emergency response. Technical plans require qualified engineers and local approval.","steps":["Document safety responsibilities and escalation contacts.","Specify maintenance, inspection and incident reporting plans.","Design accessible customer facilities and clear site signage."]},{"title":"Explore mobility-adjacent services","text":"Convenience retail, rest areas and future charging infrastructure can be assessed using customer needs, utility constraints and lifecycle costs.","steps":["Compare service options and capital commitments.","Model utilization with conservative demand assumptions.","Pilot suitable low-risk retail and support services first."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Does Moj Play Win sell fuel here?","answer":"No. This is an industry overview, not a fuel-sales or licensed-service offer."},{"question":"Can this page replace a regulatory feasibility study?","answer":"No. Site-specific safety, environmental and licensing assessments are essential."}],"links":[{"label":"Industry","url":"/industry/"},{"label":"Economy","url":"/economy/"}]},"venture:jewelry-gold":{"intro":"Jewelry presentation should celebrate craft while giving buyers verifiable information about materials, dimensions and provenance. This guide explores quality communication and responsible digital retail, not precious-metal price quotations.","chapters":[{"title":"Document workmanship and materials","text":"Record alloy or purity testing where supported, stone descriptions, dimensions, repairs and production methods. Avoid claims about certification without documentary evidence.","steps":["Write a consistent product specification and care instructions.","Use accurate images from multiple angles when a real item exists.","Keep assay and gemstone grading documents linked to the relevant item."]},{"title":"Explain price components clearly","text":"Separate material weight, workmanship, stones, tax and other applicable charges. Market-sensitive prices need their own dated source and clear conditions.","steps":["Define the units and basis of each stated price.","Record fees, delivery conditions and return limitations.","Verify any claimed hallmark or independent evaluation."]},{"title":"Build a trustworthy jewelry catalog","text":"A polished visual identity cannot replace accurate stock, secure delivery and customer support. Show purchase actions only where ownership and fulfillment are verified.","steps":["Organize collections with genuine, nonrepeating product photos.","Display sizing, availability and fulfillment information.","Review privacy and order handling before activating transactions."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Are these live gold prices?","answer":"No. This page is an educational and design overview. Any live quotation must be sourced, dated and presented separately."},{"question":"Does a gemstone photograph prove authenticity?","answer":"No. Authentication and grading require appropriate professional methods and documentation."}],"links":[{"label":"Digital market","url":"/market/"},{"label":"Economics","url":"/economy/"}]},"venture:carpets":{"intro":"Handwoven textiles carry design, technique and regional heritage that deserve careful documentation. A useful carpet guide explains materials, weaving structure, condition, care and reliable online catalog practices.","chapters":[{"title":"Recognize craft and construction","text":"Describe warp, weft, knotting, pile, fiber and dye characteristics without inferring an exact origin solely from a pattern. Distinguish documented provenance from stylistic resemblance.","steps":["Record measurements, materials and construction details.","Photograph front, back, edges and condition of a real piece.","Preserve any maker history and supporting documentation."]},{"title":"Assess condition and long-term care","text":"Light exposure, humidity, storage and prior repairs affect condition. Cleaning and conservation methods should be chosen according to material and dye stability.","steps":["Document stains, wear and repairs transparently.","Recommend appropriate storage and handling precautions.","Refer uncertain restoration decisions to experienced conservators."]},{"title":"Create an honest online catalog","text":"A responsible listing includes accurate dimensions, condition, detailed images and realistic shipping expectations. Avoid guaranteeing age or geographic origin without evidence.","steps":["Describe the exact item rather than a generic category.","State condition and provenance evidence clearly.","Explain packing, delivery and support before a sale."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Can motif alone establish where a carpet was made?","answer":"No. Motifs travel across regions; materials, technique, documented history and expert examination provide stronger evidence."},{"question":"Are the carpets displayed here for sale?","answer":"This overview does not claim verified live inventory or active checkout."}],"links":[{"label":"Knowledge","url":"/knowledge/"},{"label":"Market","url":"/market/"}]},"venture:currency-crypto":{"intro":"Currency and digital-asset education requires precise terminology, technical awareness and serious discussion of risk. This resource is informational, not an invitation to trade, purchase or transfer funds.","chapters":[{"title":"Understand different market instruments","text":"Distinguish national currencies, payment tokens, public blockchains, wallets and custody models. Price movement, liquidity and counterparty risk differ across instruments.","steps":["Define the instrument and how its value is measured.","Separate exchange operation from wallet ownership and settlement.","Check which rules apply in the relevant jurisdiction."]},{"title":"Learn blockchain transaction basics","text":"Transfers involve addresses, network fees, confirmations and irreversible errors. A wallet address alone does not prove who owns an account or that a payment has been reconciled.","steps":["Use network-specific terminology and test environments when learning.","Verify transaction status from authoritative infrastructure.","Understand phishing, key loss and smart-contract risk."]},{"title":"Analyze uncertainty without promises","text":"Volatility, liquidity, operational outages and evolving rules matter alongside technology. Distinguish educational examples from live market prices and financial advice.","steps":["Record price source and timestamp for any quoted value.","Explain both upside and downside scenarios.","Avoid return guarantees or unsupported token recommendations."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Can this page exchange or custody digital assets?","answer":"No. It is an educational overview, not an exchange, brokerage or custody service."},{"question":"Are blockchain transfers reversible?","answer":"Typically not by the network itself. Mistaken transfers may be unrecoverable; verify the network and recipient carefully."}],"links":[{"label":"Economy","url":"/economy/"},{"label":"Knowledge","url":"/knowledge/"}]},"venture:ecommerce":{"intro":"Digital commerce brings together a clear catalog, trustworthy checkout, verified delivery and ongoing customer support. This guide separates business-design concepts from products actually available for purchase.","chapters":[{"title":"Design product discovery around customer questions","text":"Give each offer an accurate name, audience, compatibility, examples and limitations. Use accessible navigation and avoid presenting several editorial cards as verified inventory.","steps":["Create structured categories and unique product previews.","Write product details and licensing terms in plain language.","Validate internal links and device compatibility."]},{"title":"Protect payments and entitlements","text":"Existing wallets, prices, customer orders and fulfillment records must be preserved. Test payment confirmation and duplicate prevention before claiming a new checkout works.","steps":["Inventory protected products and payment configurations.","Test reconciliation and delivery in an authorized safe environment.","Make refund, support and error handling clear."]},{"title":"Improve fulfillment and repeat usefulness","text":"Digital downloads, subscriptions and consulting each require different confirmation and support processes. Measure whether customers actually receive what they expected.","steps":["Provide useful installation or usage instructions.","Document license access and recovery.","Review delivery failures without disclosing user data."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Is every card an active commercial offer?","answer":"No. Verify the authoritative catalog and checkout before attempting purchase; educational examples are not live inventory."},{"question":"Does the guide change any existing crypto wallet?","answer":"No. It is informational content and does not modify payment or wallet infrastructure."}],"links":[{"label":"Market","url":"/market/"},{"label":"Store","url":"/store/"}]},"venture:hospitality":{"intro":"Hospitality experience is built from dependable service design, accessible information and thoughtful operations. This overview connects guest needs with digital systems while avoiding unverified claims about hotels or venues.","chapters":[{"title":"Map the end-to-end guest journey","text":"Start with discovery, inquiry, arrival, service, payment and support. Identify where customers need clear information, accessible options or personal assistance.","steps":["Describe the target guest and expected service.","Document every handoff between staff and systems.","Identify preventable delays and points of confusion."]},{"title":"Make operational quality measurable","text":"Use checklists, staff training, hygiene practices and documented complaint handling. Sensitive guest information should be collected only where required for service.","steps":["Define quality and response-time indicators.","Create escalation paths for service failures.","Review accessibility, safety and local compliance."]},{"title":"Introduce digital tools responsibly","text":"Booking systems, messaging, menus and loyalty programs work only when they reflect real availability and accountable staff workflows.","steps":["Verify availability before exposing a reservation action.","State communication and privacy expectations.","Pilot a small service workflow and measure actual results."]}],"faqs":[{"question":"Is this a hotel or restaurant booking website?","answer":"No. This is a service-design overview and does not claim any bookable rooms, tables or live operating venues."},{"question":"What improves service most?","answer":"Clear customer information, reliable staff handoffs, safe processes and a way to respond when the experience fails."}],"links":[{"label":"Company","url":"/company/"},{"label":"Cafes and restaurants","url":"/ventures/cafe-restaurant/"}]}}''')
